Dr. Joram Aniya, Member, NITI Aayog, addressed a lecture on “Indigenous Knowledge Systems and Viksit Bharat@2047” at the Institute of Bioresources and Sustainable Development (IBSD), Imphal.



She emphasised the need to preserve, scientifically validate and strengthen indigenous knowledge, particularly in areas such as sustainable agriculture, biodiversity conservation and natural resource management.



Highlighting the Apatani agricultural system of Ziro, Arunachal Pradesh, Dr. Aniya underscored how modern science and technology can complement traditional practices while keeping local communities at the centre.



During the visit, she also released a compendium on medicinal plants of the Zingiberaceae family in Northeast India and visited the Genome Sequencing Facility at IBSD.



The engagement reaffirmed the value of integrating indigenous knowledge, modern science and community participation towards Viksit Bharat@2047.



