Dr. Joram Aniya, Member, NITI Aayog, and Dr. Krishnananda Samurailatpam Sharma, Adviser (Policy Matter) to CM, Manipur, accompanied by senior officials of NITI Aayog and the Government of Manipur, visited key cultural, sporting and tourism destinations in Imphal.



At Ima Keithel market, Dr. Aniya interacted with women vendors, understanding their livelihoods and infrastructure needs, highlighting the importance of strengthening support systems for this iconic women-led marketplace.



At Mapal Kangjeibung Polo Ground, interactions with polo players highlighted Manipur’s rich sporting heritage. At Marjing Polo Complex, discussions centred on the State’s Sagol Kangjei legacy and opportunities to leverage technology and immersive experiences such as Augmented Reality to promote polo heritage and tourism.



The engagements reflected Manipur’s immense potential across women-led enterprise, sports, culture and tourism.



