Shri Rajiv Gauba, Member, NITI Aayog, addressed the plenary session on “Regulatory Oversight in an Age of Disruption” at the 5th Kautilya Economic Conclave, highlighting the need for regulatory frameworks to evolve alongside rapid geopolitical, technological and economic changes.



He emphasised that the challenge is not to choose between regulation and growth, but to develop regulations that manage risks while supporting innovation, competition and investment.



He also highlighted the need for regulatory independence alongside accountability, stronger regulatory capacity and specialised expertise, as well as greater coordination among regulators to address overlapping mandates and regulatory gaps.



Shri Gauba said the goal should be a State that is “firm where risks are high, and light-touch where risks are low,” while remaining predictable in both cases. He linked this approach to sustaining the high growth needed for Viksit Bharat by 2047, consistent with the vision of Trust Based Governance or Jan Vishwas.



